I built the sprint board in plain TypeScript and DOM, in `src/main.ts` (default-exported `mount`), `src/board.ts`, `src/archive.ts`, `src/dom.ts` and `src/styles.ts`. `./check` passes and all 26 visible tests pass (6 of 15 runs used). I was unsure about a few choices the brief leaves open: move, add and checklist-add buttons are disabled while their target column or checklist is still loading, a declined move that overlaps another move on the same card may leave it in a slightly wrong position, and the rename input keeps its text after a rename.